Additive, self-contained. Exposes the raw Brandt mass pairing (the diagonal
inner product InnerProductMatrixBig computes internally) as a public intrinsic,
so the Delta' computation can read the monodromy pairing in the same basis as
InternalHMFRawHeckeDefiniteSparse. Apply on top of hmf-sparse-hecke.patch.

REVISED 2026-08-31: the first version called InnerProductMatrixBig(M) and read
the diagonal off the returned matrix.  That function stores the diagonal
SPARSELY but its `return Matrix(...)` densifies it to dim x dim — 95+ GB at
level q0 (dim 109240) — which killed the first q0 run at the 40 GB cap.  The
intrinsic now replicates the weight-2 mass computation (definite.m,
InnerProductMatrixBig, lines ~770-783 verbatim) and returns only the diagonal.
Regression check: level 31 gives N = 1461, masses {1,3}, sum 4365, identical
to the old path.

Two changes to ModFrmHil/definite.m:

1. A forward declaration, next to the existing `forward HeckeOperatorDefiniteBig;`
   (kept for documentation/possible future use; the revised intrinsic no longer
   calls InnerProductMatrixBig, and it uses get_rids — imported at the top of
   definite.m — and HilbertModularSpaceDirectFactors — forward-declared at
   line ~75 already):

     forward HeckeOperatorDefiniteBig;
    +forward InnerProductMatrixBig;

2. A new intrinsic, immediately after InternalHMFRawHeckeDefiniteSparse
   (i.e. right before `intrinsic HeckeMatrixRaw`):

+intrinsic InternalHMFRawInnerProductDefinite(M::ModFrmHil) -> SeqEnum
+{The diagonal Brandt mass pairing on the raw space containing M (the natural
+ Hecke-invariant inner product), returned as the sequence of diagonal masses in
+ the same basis as InternalHMFRawHeckeDefiniteSparse.  Parallel weight 2 only.
+ This is the monodromy pairing on the character lattice of the Cerednik-Drinfeld
+ toric reduction (dembele/certificates/gate5-delta-prime-plan.md).}
+
+  require not assigned M`Ambient :
+         "This space is computed as a subspace of another space: use M`Ambient";
+  require Seqset(Weight(M)) eq {2} :
+         "Only implemented for parallel weight 2";
+
+  // The mass computation of InnerProductMatrixBig, WITHOUT calling it: its
+  // `return Matrix(...)` densifies the diagonal to dim x dim (95 GB at level
+  // q0, dim 109240).  Only the diagonal is ever needed.
+  easy := Level(M) eq Discriminant(QuaternionOrder(M));
+  rids := get_rids(M);
+  unit_orders := [#UnitGroup(LeftOrder(I)) : I in rids];
+  ulcm := LCM(unit_orders);
+  if easy then
+    masses := [Integers()| ulcm div u : u in unit_orders];
+  else
+    HMDFs := HilbertModularSpaceDirectFactors(M); assert #HMDFs eq #rids;
+    masses := [Integers()| ulcm div x : x in HMDFs[i]`PLD`StabOrders, i in [1..#rids]];
+  end if;
+  masses := [Integers()| x div g : x in masses] where g is GCD(masses);
+  return masses;
+end intrinsic;

REVISED AGAIN 2026-08-31 (second intrinsic): the Eichler-mass diagonal above is
NOT the Hecke-self-adjoint pairing.  Empirically (level 1, N = 58): with the
masses W, W_i T_ij = W_j T_ji fails on 304 of 1197 support entries; the unique
consistent diagonal (derived from T's entry ratios along the support graph,
verified globally) is the RECIPROCAL pattern W'_i = (ulcm/g)/W_i = e_i, the
stabilizer orders — the classical Brandt relation e_j T_ij = e_i T_ji and the
Cerednik-Drinfeld monodromy edge lengths.  A third intrinsic exposes them:

+intrinsic InternalHMFRawStabOrdersDefinite(M::ModFrmHil) -> SeqEnum, RngIntElt, RngIntElt
+{The stabilizer orders e_i on the raw space containing M, in the same basis as
+ InternalHMFRawHeckeDefiniteSparse, plus ulcm = LCM(e_i) and g = the GCD the
+ mass normalization divides by.  The Brandt relation is e_j T_ij = e_i T_ji,
+ so diag(e) — NOT the Eichler-mass diagonal ulcm/(g e_i) of
+ InternalHMFRawInnerProductDefinite, which is its reciprocal up to the constant
+ ulcm/g — is the Hecke-self-adjoint pairing and the Cerednik-Drinfeld
+ monodromy pairing's edge lengths.  Parallel weight 2 only.}
+
+  require not assigned M`Ambient :
+         "This space is computed as a subspace of another space: use M`Ambient";
+  require Seqset(Weight(M)) eq {2} :
+         "Only implemented for parallel weight 2";
+
+  easy := Level(M) eq Discriminant(QuaternionOrder(M));
+  rids := get_rids(M);
+  unit_orders := [#UnitGroup(LeftOrder(I)) : I in rids];
+  ulcm := LCM(unit_orders);
+  if easy then
+    stabs := unit_orders;
+  else
+    HMDFs := HilbertModularSpaceDirectFactors(M); assert #HMDFs eq #rids;
+    stabs := [Integers()| x : x in HMDFs[i]`PLD`StabOrders, i in [1..#rids]];
+  end if;
+  g := GCD([Integers()| ulcm div e : e in stabs]);
+  return stabs, ulcm, g;
+end intrinsic;
